{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,10]],"date-time":"2026-09-10T20:11:58Z","timestamp":1789071118073,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":62,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"21","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,10]],"date-time":"2026-04-10T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1775779200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,10]],"date-time":"2026-04-10T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1775779200000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/doi.wiley.com\/10.1002\/tdm_license_1.1"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001809","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["22472122"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["22472122"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001809","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["22332004"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["22332004"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001809","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["22272122"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["22272122"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100012166","name":"National Key Research and Development Program of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["2023YFA1509004"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["2023YFA1509004"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100012166","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Angew Chem Int Ed"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,18]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    Precisely deciphering the intrinsic origin of the high overpotential for oxygen evolution reaction (OER), even on the most active RuO\n                    <jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub>\n                    catalysts, remains a long\u2010standing challenge in electrocatalysis. Herein, by meticulously elucidating the electrode charging behavior, oxygenated surface phases and interfacial double\u2010layer structures under OER\u2010relevant potentials on RuO\n                    <jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub>\n                    (110), together with their impact on reaction pathways and elementary\u2010step energetics through ab\u2010initio molecular dynamics simulations, we reveal that the high overpotential jointly arises from the pronounced surface negative charge, due to the unusually high potential of zero charge, and the excessive protonation of surface\u2010active *O at coordinatively unsaturated Ru sites (*O\n                    <jats:sub>CUS<\/jats:sub>\n                    ) at low potentials (&lt;1.60\u00a0V). This, on one hand, severely depletes active *O\n                    <jats:sub>CUS<\/jats:sub>\n                    intermediate, thereby suppressing the rate\u2010determining step (RDS) of oxide pathway mechanism (OPM), necessarily involving surface O\u2500O coupling between two *O\n                    <jats:sub>CUS<\/jats:sub>\n                    via Langmuir\u2010Hinshelwood mechanism. On the other hand, it induces the dense, strongly hydrogen\u2010bonded interfacial water layer that, together with electrostatic repulsion, obstructs the essential water reorientation and approach for the RDS of adsorbate evolution mechanism (AEM), featuring incoming interfacial water to reorient and react with *O\n                    <jats:sub>CUS<\/jats:sub>\n                    via Eley\u2010Rideal\u2010like mechanism. Furthermore, a potential\u2010dependent mechanistic switching between AEM and OPM is identified, dictated by their distinct RDS natures and kinetic sensitivities.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/anie.202521856","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,11]],"date-time":"2026-04-11T05:27:11Z","timestamp":1775885231000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":3,"title":["Potential\u2010Dependent Oxygenated Surface Phases and Interfacial Water Layers Underlie the High Overpotential and Mechanistic Switching of Oxygen Evolution on RuO\n                    <sub>2<\/sub>"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"65","author":[{"given":"Peimeng","family":"Qiu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Hubei Key Laboratory of Electrochemical Power Sources, College of Chemistry and Molecular Sciences Wuhan University  Wuhan Hubei P.R. China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Yuzhou","family":"Jiao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Hubei Key Laboratory of Electrochemical Power Sources, College of Chemistry and Molecular Sciences Wuhan University  Wuhan Hubei P.R. China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Jingyi","family":"Hu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Hubei Key Laboratory of Electrochemical Power Sources, College of Chemistry and Molecular Sciences Wuhan University  Wuhan Hubei P.R. China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7448-8860","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Shengli","family":"Chen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Hubei Key Laboratory of Electrochemical Power Sources, College of Chemistry and Molecular Sciences Wuhan University  Wuhan Hubei P.R. China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0438-7209","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Peng","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Hubei Key Laboratory of Electrochemical Power Sources, College of Chemistry and Molecular Sciences Wuhan University  Wuhan Hubei P.R. China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,10]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_7_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/nature11475"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1126\/science.aad4998"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1126\/science.ado9938"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.esci.2024.100307"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1126\/science.adk9849"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/adma.202006328"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.13208\/j.electrochem.2214010"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_9_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/adfm.202509656"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_10_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/jacs.5c01886"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_11_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/adma.202503354"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_12_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1039\/D4EE05220J"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_13_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.chemphys.2005.05.038"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_14_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/cctc.201000397"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_15_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41560\u2010024\u201001583\u2010x"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_16_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/jacs.1c01655"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_17_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/acs.jpcb.7b06982"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_18_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/acscatal.1c03290"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_19_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/adma.202500449"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_20_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1039\/D4EE02549K"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_21_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.26599\/NR.2025.94907589"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_22_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.c